WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:03.230
- We're just beginning the
investigation into what gave rise

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:07.010
to the January 6th
attack on the US Capitol.

00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:10.060
But what we're learning
is that this was no fluke.

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:12.650
This was planned in
advance from everywhere

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:15.530
from Instagram to
Facebook, to the dark web.

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:17.160
And this wasn't just idle chatter

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:20.520
from some rando on a
conspiracy theory forum though.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.740
They certainly participated as well.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:25.350
No, a lot of these people
were middle-class Americans

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:29.240
who just contracted brain worms
from Newsmax, OAN, Fox News

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:31.600
and sometimes even their
relatives on Facebook.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:34.520
And while it's certainly possible
that some of these people

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:36.930
never thought that it would
get out of hand the way it did

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:39.060
a lot of these people
planned it ahead of time.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:41.890
And what unifies all of
these people together

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:43.550
is that they are all going to face

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:45.780
incredibly harsh criminal sentences

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.730
for some of the things
that they perpetrated

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:49.830
whether they intended to do it or not.

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:52.990
And while some of the perpetrators
flew in on a private jet

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:55.240
and are now asking for
a presidential pardon,

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:58.050
let's talk about what
crimes all of these rioters

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.083
and their leaders might be charged with.

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:05.123
Hey, legal Eagles.

00:01:05.123 --> 00:01:07.580
It's time to think like
a criminal defense lawyer

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:10.600
because a lot of these
rioters are going to need one.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:13.360
Now, before I dive into
the litany of crimes

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:15.080
that these writers might face

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:16.710
there are two general considerations

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:19.240
that I think are particularly
interesting here.

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:22.050
The first is that a lot of
people have been surprised

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:23.650
at the relatively light charges

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.130
that have been levied so far.

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:27.340
So far hundreds have been charged

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:30.150
and probably hundreds more
will be charged as well.

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:32.810
But people have been surprised
at the types of crimes

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:34.100
that they've been charged with,

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.770
many face lesser charges,
such as unlawful entry,

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:39.380
disorderly conduct and
defacing public property,

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:42.490
and only a few have been accused
of the more serious crimes

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:44.600
like felony violations of the right act.

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:46.920
And we're gonna talk about
that in just a second.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:49.660
But one thing that is overlooked here is

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:51.550
that these might not be the final charges.

00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:54.210
It's pretty common for
authorities to make arrest based

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:58.520
on readily proven charges in
this case such as trespassing.

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:00.780
And then weeks later prosecutors can seek

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:04.220
a grand jury indictment
on more serious charges.

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:05.370
And a lot of this has to do with the way

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:06.900
that federal courts operate

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:09.540
because in order to charge
someone with a felony,

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:11.920
you have to go before a grand jury,

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:15.790
a grand jury although it
has a very grand title is

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:18.460
really just a group of individuals

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:21.080
that act as a check on
prosecutorial power.

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:23.370
Even before things go to trial,

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:25.150
generally speaking a district attorney,

00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:27.070
or in this case a US
attorney would have to go

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:28.460
before a grand jury and say,

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:31.820
here's the probable cause
for me to indict a criminal.

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:34.620
And only after the grand jury signs off

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:35.880
on that particular proceeding

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:39.240
can you then indict someone
for a felony charge?

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:41.580
One way around that is
a US attorney can swear

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:44.620
an affidavit of probable
cause to a magistrate judge

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:46.640
and get what's called a criminal complaint

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:47.790
to start the proceedings

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:50.600
and avoid having to convene a grand jury.

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:53.220
You basically start the
process by complaint

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:54.410
and you can get a complaint

00:02:54.410 --> 00:02:56.540
for either a misdemeanor
charge or a felony.

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:57.600
But the difference is that,

00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:59.190
while you can charge a misdemeanor

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:02.410
without ever going to a grand
jury, generally for a felony

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:04.850
you have to go in front of a grand jury

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:08.810
within 30 days of getting
that criminal complaint.

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:11.580
Now, there are two main
reasons why you might wanna use

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:14.290
the complaint process and might
explain some of the things

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:16.030
that we're seeing with
respect to the rioters.

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:17.910
The first is that some jurisdictions don't

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:20.280
actually have a grand
jury convened right now

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:22.570
because of COVID related reasons.

00:03:22.570 --> 00:03:25.040
And the other is that you
might use a criminal complaint

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:27.300
to get someone into the court system

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:29.840
to get them under the court supervision

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:30.930
so that you can go back

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:33.210
and charge more serious things later.

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:35.080
So with the initial charges filed

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:37.440
the federal prosecutor might
go before a grand jury later

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:40.210
and then seek significantly
more serious crimes.

00:03:40.210 --> 00:03:43.190
And even then once there
is a formal indictment

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:44.940
you can always convene a grand jury

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:46.450
to get a superseding indictment

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:48.720
and charge them with
even more serious crimes.

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:50.900
So if you are a Capitol rioter

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:53.060
and you think you're
off relatively scot-free

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:56.130
because you were just charged
with misdemeanor trespass

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:59.270
more serious charges may
definitely be on the way.

00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:02.190
Now, the other issue that
I think is overarching here

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:03.850
is the issue of conspiracy,

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:06.330
because a lot of these people
coordinated with each other

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:09.700
both before they attacked and
laid siege to the Capitol.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:12.180
And then even while they
were in the midst of it

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:14.310
certain people coordinate with each other.

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:17.130
There is truly a federal
conspiracy statute

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:18.160
but for the most part

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:21.300
that's an add on to other
and different crimes.

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:23.960
People have to agree to some sort of crime

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:26.010
and there has to be a meeting of the minds

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:28.580
but you can't conspire to
do something not illegal.

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:29.670
You can't conspire

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:31.500
with your friends to go
have dinner together.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:34.340
That's not a crime, I
guess unless you're talking

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.590
about COVID risks, but
let's put that aside.

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:39.240
You cannot conspire to do
something that's not a crime

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:42.350
but the benefit of charging
someone with conspiracy

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:44.990
from a federal prosecutor's
perspective is that,

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:47.820
you don't actually have to
complete the crime to be guilty.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.990
You just have to take one overt act

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:52.350
in furtherance of that conspiracy

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:55.410
or in furtherance of that
ultimate criminal end.

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:58.288
So if there are
circumstances that give rise

00:04:58.288 --> 00:05:00.030
to an agreement, a meeting of the mind

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:02.690
where people take at
least one step toward it,

00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:05.657
then effectively all of the
people who are participating

00:05:05.657 --> 00:05:09.450
in the conspiracy can
face penalties that are

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:13.210
basically the same as the
initial underlying crime itself.

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:15.660
So we're just about to talk
about all the different crimes

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.340
that all these people
might have committed.

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:19.930
But on top of that, if
any particular person

00:05:19.930 --> 00:05:21.870
regardless of what individual crimes

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:23.010
they might've committed themselves,

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.600
if they agreed to participate

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:26.710
in a conspiracy to commit
one of these crimes

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:29.820
they could be guilty of
that conspiracy as well.

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:30.930
But with that understanding,

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:34.210
let's dive into the actual
crimes that the Capitol rioters

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:35.530
might be facing.

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:37.840
Now, of course, there were
a lot of people there doing

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:39.020
a lot of a legal things.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:41.620
So not everyone is
likely to have committed

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:43.990
one of these crimes, but
this is sort of a smattering

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:46.260
of the things that they're likely to face.

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:48.200
And the first is the word,

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:49.540
that you've probably been hearing

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:51.720
a lot these days and that is sedition

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:54.250
in particular a seditious conspiracy found

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:58.010
in 18 U.S.C. section 2384

00:05:58.010 --> 00:05:58.950
which states that if two

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:01.210
or more persons conspired
to overthrow, put down

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:03.460
or destroy by force the
government of the United States

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:04.690
or to levy war against them,

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:07.400
or to oppose by force
the authority thereof

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:08.980
or by force to prevent hinder

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:12.890
or delay the execution of any
law or by force to seize take

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:16.070
or possess any property
of the United States.

00:06:16.070 --> 00:06:18.070
Now we have covered the law of sedition

00:06:18.070 --> 00:06:20.090
and treason many times on this channel.

00:06:20.090 --> 00:06:22.320
And at this point, you're
probably sick of hearing me talk

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:23.960
about how it's not sedition.

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:27.290
It's never a sedition that
these people are guilty of.

00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:30.780
Well, congratulations, because
this is not the same case.

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:34.900
This is probably a slam dunk
for many of the rioters.

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:36.780
They probably committed sedition

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:39.920
because lots and lots of people stormed

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:42.670
the Capitol clearly used force.

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:45.010
Specifically they tried
to prevent Congress

00:06:45.010 --> 00:06:46.420
from certifying the election

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:48.130
and certifying that Joe Biden is

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:50.000
the president of the United States.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:52.110
If that's not using force to oppose

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:55.340
a law of the United States,
I'm not sure I know what it is.

00:06:55.340 --> 00:06:58.160
So despite the fact that
it's never a sedition

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:00.630
here it's probably sedition.

00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:03.020
And by the way, because
the events of January were

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:05.450
so excited credibly preposterous

00:07:05.450 --> 00:07:07.070
that's the legal term.

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:09.310
I've noticed a ton of new
people coming to the channel

00:07:09.310 --> 00:07:11.810
but only a small number
are actually subscribed.

00:07:11.810 --> 00:07:13.510
So if you enjoy this legal analysis,

00:07:13.510 --> 00:07:15.730
and I wanna see me lose my
mind over the next thing

00:07:15.730 --> 00:07:18.690
I'll have to explain as a
lawyer, make sure you subscribe,

00:07:18.690 --> 00:07:20.590
but there's actually an interesting Coda

00:07:20.590 --> 00:07:22.620
to this whole sedition conspiracy thing

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:25.400
which is that in September of 2020,

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:28.540
the DOJ created a memo
which actually recommended

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:31.620
charging protesters with section 2384.

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:33.700
The only thing is that
those protestors were

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:36.270
the BLM protestors over the summer.

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:37.770
The memo was authorized

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:39.960
by former attorney
general Bill Barr signed

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:42.290
by now acting attorney
general Jeffrey Rosen.

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:44.190
And they intended it to be used

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:46.760
against black lives matter
protesters and Tifa.

00:07:46.760 --> 00:07:49.310
And the memo goes on to
recommend charging protesters

00:07:49.310 --> 00:07:53.610
with violations of 18 U.S.C.
1361 damage to federal property

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:57.050
18 U.S.C. 844 use of fire or explosives

00:07:57.050 --> 00:08:02.050
18 U.S.C. 231a civil disorder,
18 U.S.C. 2101 a riots.

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:05.000
18 U.S.C. 875 interstate communications

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:08.460
18 U.S.C. 1369 damage
to veteran's monuments

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:12.300
and 18 U.S.C. 1952
interstate foreign travel

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:15.590
or transport patient in aid
of racketeering enterprises.

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:19.250
And no, I am not going to
cover Rico in this video

00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:22.270
but this memo is a
really interesting lesson

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:24.550
that all of these things
that are on the books

00:08:24.550 --> 00:08:26.040
can be charged in circumstances

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:27.890
that you may or may not agree with.

00:08:27.890 --> 00:08:30.270
And while a lot of people
want to throw the book

00:08:30.270 --> 00:08:31.940
at the Capitol rioters,

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:33.960
perhaps they might not feel as strongly

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:36.150
about throwing the book at the protestors

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:38.110
over the summer who supported BLM.

00:08:38.110 --> 00:08:40.390
So that takes us to the other buzzword

00:08:40.390 --> 00:08:42.130
that you've probably been hearing a lot.

00:08:42.130 --> 00:08:43.930
And that is insurrection.

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:47.440
Now that's covered in
18 U.S.C. 2383 rebellion

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:50.780
or insurrection and section
2383 makes rebellion

00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:52.150
against the United States a crime,

00:08:52.150 --> 00:08:54.940
specifically whoever
insights sets on foot assists

00:08:54.940 --> 00:08:57.140
or engages in any
rebellion or insurrection

00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:58.610
against the authority of the United States

00:08:58.610 --> 00:08:59.880
or the laws thereof

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:02.620
or gives aid or comfort
there too shall be fined

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:04.360
under this title or imprisoned.

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:07.190
Not more than 10 years or
both end shall be incapable

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:09.570
of holding office under the United States.

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:10.450
As I've covered before,

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:12.810
there are a whole bunch
of other criminal laws

00:09:12.810 --> 00:09:13.670
that apply here that are

00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:16.290
probably a better fit than rebellion.

00:09:16.290 --> 00:09:18.100
This sort of rebellion insurrection.

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:20.292
We might be splitting hairs.

00:09:20.292 --> 00:09:23.670
They're not necessarily trying
to overthrow the government.

00:09:23.670 --> 00:09:26.580
They're just trying to
change the government

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:27.980
from their perspective.

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:29.880
So arguably I don't think this fits

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:31.230
unless they did something really stupid

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:33.122
like claiming it was a revolution.

00:09:33.122 --> 00:09:35.175
- [Interview] Why did you wanna go in?

00:09:35.175 --> 00:09:36.970
- We're storming the Capitol.

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:38.160
It's a revolution

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:40.633
- Come on.

00:09:41.750 --> 00:09:46.590
But arguably the same arguments
apply to 18 U.S.C. 2385

00:09:46.590 --> 00:09:48.960
which is advocating the
overthrow of the government

00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:51.790
though a lot of people did
some incredibly stupid things

00:09:51.790 --> 00:09:54.420
that might actually toe
the line on these ones.

00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:56.310
For example, the infamous racist known

00:09:56.310 --> 00:09:59.270
as Baked Alaska whose
real name is Tim Gionet,

00:09:59.270 --> 00:10:02.240
live streamed himself breaking
into the Capitol building

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:04.840
and called for all the
Congress members to be hung

00:10:04.840 --> 00:10:06.870
in the middle of the riot.

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:08.940
So who knows at this point,

00:10:08.940 --> 00:10:11.070
it depends on how aggressive

00:10:11.070 --> 00:10:12.600
the federal prosecutors want to be

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:15.620
and how determined they
are to get a conviction

00:10:15.620 --> 00:10:17.280
in these different cases.

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:18.113
But that takes us

00:10:18.113 --> 00:10:19.900
to another really
interesting federal statute

00:10:19.900 --> 00:10:23.600
which is the anti-riot
act in 18 U.S.C. 2101.

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:24.918
Now the anti-riot act requires

00:10:24.918 --> 00:10:27.130
that a defendant travel
in interstate commerce

00:10:27.130 --> 00:10:29.180
or use its facilities
with the intent to follow

00:10:29.180 --> 00:10:31.470
one of the objectives
listed in one through four

00:10:31.470 --> 00:10:33.860
each with a riot as the objective.

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:35.980
Now, if this crime sounds familiar,

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:38.710
it's probably because
this was the central law

00:10:38.710 --> 00:10:40.900
at issue in the trial of the Chicago seven

00:10:40.900 --> 00:10:43.330
which I just did a video
on a few weeks ago.

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:45.830
In that case, several defendants
were charged with traveling

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:47.930
to Chicago to start a riot.

00:10:47.930 --> 00:10:50.060
Count one of the indictment
against them claim

00:10:50.060 --> 00:10:51.840
that they conspired not only to travel in

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:53.870
and use the facilities
of interstate commerce

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:55.480
with the intent to insight, organize

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:57.720
and promote and encourage a riot

00:10:57.720 --> 00:11:01.010
but also to participate
in and carry on a riot

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:03.470
to commit acts of violence
and further into the riot

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:07.300
and to aid and abet
persons in such activities.

00:11:07.300 --> 00:11:08.840
But at the same time, this goes down

00:11:08.840 --> 00:11:11.160
as one of the black marks
of federal prosecutions

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:14.350
because people largely perceive this trial

00:11:14.350 --> 00:11:16.530
the Chicago seven as being a show trial

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:18.600
that was meant to punish the people

00:11:18.600 --> 00:11:20.283
who participated in protests

00:11:20.283 --> 00:11:23.290
and punish them for their
free exercise of speech.

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:26.530
And that takes us to a whole
raft of the less sexy crimes

00:11:26.530 --> 00:11:27.710
but are ones that are

00:11:27.710 --> 00:11:29.700
probably going to be complete slam dunks,

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:31.730
like the weapons charges

00:11:31.730 --> 00:11:35.600
that are found in 40 U.S.C. section 5104,

00:11:35.600 --> 00:11:37.760
which are oddly specifically tailored

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:39.470
to this particular situation

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:41.870
which says that you
cannot possess firearms

00:11:41.870 --> 00:11:43.810
and other dangerous weapons in Congress.

00:11:43.810 --> 00:11:46.760
And that you may not knowingly
with force and violence enter

00:11:46.760 --> 00:11:49.980
or remain on the floor of
either house of Congress.

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:52.360
That really seems like
it applies to people

00:11:52.360 --> 00:11:55.110
who entered the houses of Congress.

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:55.943
And then there is things

00:11:55.943 --> 00:11:58.960
like assault on federal
officers in 18 U.S.C. 1114

00:11:58.960 --> 00:12:02.120
that makes it a crime to kill
or attempt to kill any officer

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:04.290
or employee of the United States

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:06.880
or illegally possessing
a dangerous firearm

00:12:06.880 --> 00:12:10.050
on any federal facility in 18 U.S.C. 930.

00:12:10.050 --> 00:12:11.870
And then of course it
should surprise no one

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:13.250
that there's a whole bunch of laws

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:15.360
that prevent the destruction
of federal property.

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:16.890
And then of course there is perhaps

00:12:16.890 --> 00:12:19.470
the most on the nose law in all of this is

00:12:19.470 --> 00:12:22.000
18 U.S.C. 351 congressional cabinet

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:25.130
and Supreme court assassination,
kidnapping and assault

00:12:25.130 --> 00:12:27.710
which it should surprise
no one makes it a crime

00:12:27.710 --> 00:12:30.960
to assassinate, kidnap or
assault members of Congress,

00:12:30.960 --> 00:12:33.390
the cabinet or the Supreme court.

00:12:33.390 --> 00:12:36.100
It's also illegal to
attempt to do these things.

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:39.320
So even if you entered
Congress with the intent

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:41.720
to hurt a member of Congress,

00:12:41.720 --> 00:12:45.270
you looked around and you
couldn't find a member of Congress

00:12:45.270 --> 00:12:48.380
you're still probably guilty
of the attempt to do it.

00:12:48.380 --> 00:12:50.970
So as you can imagine, that's
real bad news for the guy

00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:54.110
that brought flex cuff
zip ties in to Congress

00:12:54.110 --> 00:12:56.250
even though he actually
wasn't able to hold

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:58.400
any particular member of Congress hostage.

00:12:58.400 --> 00:13:00.600
And then finally the
last category of crimes

00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:02.780
that are likely under these circumstances,

00:13:02.780 --> 00:13:05.570
depending on how aggressive
federal prosecutors want to be

00:13:05.570 --> 00:13:10.280
are the whole swath of
antiterrorism laws that exist.

00:13:10.280 --> 00:13:12.830
It's entirely possible that
federal prosecutors will look

00:13:12.830 --> 00:13:15.010
at this as a terrorist incident.

00:13:15.010 --> 00:13:17.630
This was a whole bunch
of people using force

00:13:17.630 --> 00:13:19.940
and firearms and explosives

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:21.740
and trying to undermine the government

00:13:21.740 --> 00:13:23.810
and achieve their political ends

00:13:23.810 --> 00:13:27.230
in an anti-democratic way
in direct contravention

00:13:27.230 --> 00:13:30.060
of the actual functioning US democracy.

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:31.410
It's entirely possible.

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:33.030
This qualifies as terrorism.

00:13:33.030 --> 00:13:34.700
And I would not be surprised,

00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:37.010
if federal prosecutors took that tack,

00:13:37.010 --> 00:13:40.150
but the bottom line is that
this is all incredibly serious

00:13:40.150 --> 00:13:41.210
and these people can be charged

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:43.030
with any number of these crimes.

